  "_about": "The Outgrow boot camp town (the user, 24 Oct: \"a test city with unorthodox angles, almost a random-like grid ... more spaced out than you would think ... circles, roundabouts, curves, straight blocks, big blocks, small blocks, tiny wedges, tiny triangles, huge triangles\"). Written by tools/suite/bootcamp.js (edit it there, not here): six lands, grid (a crooked grid: four streets at odd angles crossing, blocks of every shape), circles (a ring road and a roundabout with three spokes), curves (an S bend, and a curve backing onto a straight street at an angle), blocks (a big block turned 23 degrees and a small one turned -35), triangles (a huge triangle and a tiny one), wedges (a tiny wedge (a long thin triangle) and two streets meeting at 18 degrees). Each land laid, zoned (low density homes), grown with Outgrow on new buildings, pictured from the top; the town saved as 'PM Bootcamp' after the last. Send with: powershell -File tools/suite/Send-Suite.ps1 -File suite/scenarios/outgrow-bootcamp-make.json -Who outgrow-bootcamp",
